      "id": "g01",
      "type": "single_page",
      "question": "How do I change the address on my driving licence?",
      "answer": {
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Apply online (free of charge). You can still drive while waiting for the new licence. To apply by post instead, send a completed form D1 (or D2 for lorry/bus licences), your driving licence, original documents confirming your identity, and a passport photograph, with the correct postage. You must also update your vehicle log book (V5C), your vehicle tax Direct Debit if you pay that way, and your personalised registration number document (V750 or V778) if you have one. Failing to tell DVLA can result in a fine of up to £1,000.",
