      "question": "How long do penalty points stay on my licence?",
      "answer": {
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Most penalty points (endorsements) stay on your driving record for 4 years from the date of offence. For reckless/dangerous driving (codes DD40, DD60, DD80), offences resulting in disqualification, and code TT99, the 4 years run from the date of conviction. Some offences stay for 11 years instead, but the extracts do not say which ones.",
